1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:01,700
Imagine losing money

2
00:00:01,700 --> 00:00:02,460
to a trader

3
00:00:02,460 --> 00:00:03,551
you can't even see.

4
00:00:03,711 --> 00:00:04,750
Because in India's

5
00:00:04,750 --> 00:00:05,440
OPTIONS MARKET

6
00:00:05,440 --> 00:00:06,625
you're not just competing

7
00:00:06,625 --> 00:00:08,204
with other humans anymore.

8
00:00:08,284 --> 00:00:09,195
You're competing with

9
00:00:09,195 --> 00:00:09,805
ALGORITHMS

10
00:00:09,805 --> 00:00:11,060
that can execute trades

11
00:00:11,060 --> 00:00:12,604
in fractions of a second.

12
00:00:12,684 --> 00:00:13,345
And the numbers

13
00:00:13,345 --> 00:00:14,124
are crazy.

14
00:00:14,284 --> 00:00:15,930
According to a SEBI study

15
00:00:15,930 --> 00:00:17,000
reported by Bloomberg,

16
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:18,485
Indian retail traders lost

17
00:00:18,485 --> 00:00:20,120
around $33 BILLION

18
00:00:20,120 --> 00:00:21,490
in equity derivatives

19
00:00:21,490 --> 00:00:22,365
over four years

20
00:00:22,365 --> 00:00:24,107
through March 2025.

21
00:00:24,307 --> 00:00:25,675
At the same time,

22
00:00:25,675 --> 00:00:27,135
algorithm-driven trading companies

23
00:00:27,135 --> 00:00:28,920
made around $7 BILLION

24
00:00:28,920 --> 00:00:29,700
in gross profit

25
00:00:29,700 --> 00:00:30,995
from India's options market

26
00:00:30,995 --> 00:00:32,748
in just one financial year.

27
00:00:32,948 --> 00:00:34,065
So how do these firms

28
00:00:34,065 --> 00:00:35,236
get such an advantage?

29
00:00:35,436 --> 00:00:36,215
SPEED

30
00:00:36,375 --> 00:00:37,775
Their computers can analyse

31
00:00:37,775 --> 00:00:39,310
market data and execute trades

32
00:00:39,310 --> 00:00:40,285
in MICROSECONDS

33
00:00:40,285 --> 00:00:41,245
or even faster —

34
00:00:41,245 --> 00:00:42,370
while you're still looking

35
00:00:42,370 --> 00:00:44,050
at the chart on your phone.

36
00:00:44,150 --> 00:00:45,755
And these firms spend millions

37
00:00:45,755 --> 00:00:47,185
on technology, servers

38
00:00:47,185 --> 00:00:48,650
and ultra-fast connections

39
00:00:48,650 --> 00:00:49,855
just to gain tiny

40
00:00:49,855 --> 00:00:50,977
speed advantages.

41
00:00:51,177 --> 00:00:51,970
But here's the

42
00:00:51,970 --> 00:00:52,861
important part…

43
00:00:53,121 --> 00:00:54,630
This doesn't automatically mean

44
00:00:54,630 --> 00:00:56,230
algorithms are stealing money

45
00:00:56,230 --> 00:00:57,417
from retail traders.

46
00:00:57,537 --> 00:00:59,120
High-frequency trading can also

47
00:00:59,120 --> 00:01:00,020
improve liquidity

48
00:01:00,020 --> 00:01:01,904
and make markets more efficient.

49
00:01:02,064 --> 00:01:03,905
The bigger issue is the massive

50
00:01:03,905 --> 00:01:04,695
TECHNOLOGY GAP

51
00:01:04,695 --> 00:01:05,930
between a retail trader

52
00:01:05,930 --> 00:01:07,788
and a professional trading firm.

53
00:01:08,008 --> 00:01:09,125
So next time you see

54
00:01:09,125 --> 00:01:10,423
a stock move suddenly…

55
00:01:10,583 --> 00:01:11,327
Remember:

56
00:01:11,527 --> 00:01:12,880
There might be a machine

57
00:01:12,880 --> 00:01:13,835
trading against you

58
00:01:13,835 --> 00:01:15,180
before you even realise

59
00:01:15,180 --> 00:01:15,940
what's happening.
